# Panel 194 K0 (M-buildable-structs), lane b13-bs, 2026-10-06: C's `char` is
# `i8` in every build, since the emitter passes `-fsigned-char`, and `u8` is
# what 22 of panel 178's 50 readers wrote for it first. A `u8` field, or an
# array of `u8`, that clang refuses is told so in a note, with a `guess` fix
# writing `i8`: a guess, since the header may as well write a type wider than
# a byte. Until the sitting the note said only *the header's own width and
# sign*, naming neither `char` nor `i8`.

extern "ffi-a-char-field-declared-u8-is-told-i8.h"
    record Named tag named
        name: u8[8]  #~ ffi_field_type
        flag: u8  #~ ffi_field_type
        n: i32

function main()
    m = Named(name: [104, 105, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0], flag: 1, n: 2)
    print(m.n)
